ns for his health.","He wants to win races.","He doesn't enjoy running.","Making friends mattered more than the sport."],"answer":3,"passage_id":"P-02","audio":null,"formats":["express","balance","deep"]},{"id":"R-P-02-4","block":"reading","level":3,"type":"tfns","prompt":"Daniel's colleague is also training for the half-marathon.","options":["True","False","Not stated"],"answer":2,"passage_id":"P-02","audio":null,"formats":["express","balance","deep"]},{"id":"R-P-03-1","block":"reading","level":3,"type":"choice","prompt":"Where did they have dinner on Friday?","options":["At the hotel","At a restaurant the receptionist suggested","At a friend's house","At a cafe by the river"],"answer":1,"passage_id":"P-03","audio":null,"formats":["express","balance","deep"]},{"id":"R-P-03-2","block":"reading","level":3,"type":"tfns","prompt":"They found a cafe while they were walking back.","options":["True","False","Not stated"],"answer":0,"passage_id":"P-03","audio":null,"formats":["express","balance","deep"]},{"id":"R-P-03-3","block":"reading","level":3,"type":"choice","prompt":"Why did they walk back on Saturday?","options":["The tram was too crowded.","They were lost.","The tram was too expensive.","It was raining."],"answer":0,"passage_id":"P-03","audio":null,"formats":["express","balance","deep"]},{"id":"R-P-03-4","block":"reading","level":3,"type":"tfns","prompt":"They visited a museum on Sunday.","options":["True","False","Not stated"],"answer":2,"passage_id":"P-03","audio":null,"formats":["express","balance","deep"]},{"id":"R-P-04-1","block":"reading","level":4,"type":"choice","prompt":"What does recent research suggest about sleep?","options":["Deep sleep is unnecessary.","Memory is unaffected by sleep.","Everyone needs eight hours.","It plays a bigger role in memory than assumed."],"answer":3,"passage_id":"P-04","audio":null,"formats":["express","balance","deep"]},{"id":"R-P-04-2","block":"reading","level":4,"type":"tfns","prompt":"The brain seems to replay the day's events during deep sleep.","options":["True","False","Not stated"],"answer":0,"passage_id":"P-04","audio":null,"formats":["express","balance","deep"]},{"id":"R-P-04-3","block":"reading","level":4,"type":"choice","prompt":"What do the researchers warn?","options":["Conclusions are always simple.","Sleep needs differ between people.","Revising at night is best.","Six hours is never enough."],"answer":1,"passage_id":"P-04","audio":null,"formats":["express","balance","deep"]},{"id":"R-P-04-4","block":"reading","level":4,"type":"tfns","prompt":"Most adults sleep for less than six hours a night.","options":["True","False","Not stated"],"answer":2,"passage_id":"P-04","audio":null,"formats":["express","balance","deep"]},{"id":"R-P-05-1","block":"reading","level":5,"type":"choice","prompt":"What is the writer's attitude to blaming smartphones?","options":["It is entirely justified.","It is outdated.","It is hypocritical.","It oversimplifies the issue."],"answer":3,"passage_id":"P-05","audio":null,"formats":["express","balance","deep"]},{"id":"R-P-05-2","block":"reading","level":5,"type":"tfns","prompt":"The writer claims that attention has become a limited resource only recently.","options":["True","False","Not stated"],"answer":1,"passage_id":"P-05","audio":null,"formats":["express","balance","deep"]},{"id":"R-P-05-3","block":"reading","level":5,"type":"choice","prompt":"What does the writer conclude?","options":["Users should simply try harder.","Technology should be banned.","Willpower is the best defence.","Designers share the responsibility."],"answer":3,"passage_id":"P-05","audio":null,"formats":["express","balance","deep"]},{"id":"R-P-05-4","block":"reading","level":5,"type":"tfns","prompt":"Apps are deliberately designed to keep people engaged.","options":["True","False","Not stated"],"answer":0,"passage_id":"P-05","audio":null,"formats":["express","balance","deep"]},{"id":"L-A1-001","block":"listening","level":1,"type":"choice","prompt":"Where does Kate work?","options":["In a shop","In a school","In a hospital","In a cafe"],"answer":0,"passage_id":null,"audio":"A-l01","formats":["express","balance","deep"]},{"id":"L-A1-002","block":"listening","level":1,"type":"choice","prompt":"How much is the bag?","options":["22 pounds","50 pounds","12 pounds","20 pounds"],"answer":3,"passage_id":null,"audio":"A-l02","formats":["express","balance","deep"]},{"id":"L-A2-001","block":"listening","level":2,"type":"choice","prompt":"When will they meet?","options":["At seven","At six","At half past seven","At eight"],"answer":0,"passage_id":null,"audio":"A-l03","formats":["express","balance","deep"]},{"id":"L-A2-002","block":"listening","level":2,"type":"choice","prompt":"Why can't Ben come to the gym?","options":["He is on holiday.","He is ill.","He has to work late.","He forgot."],"answer":2,"passage_id":null,"audio":"A-l04","formats":["express","balance","deep"]},{"id":"L-A2-003","block":"listening","level":2,"type":"choice","prompt":"How long is the delay?","options":["30 minutes","40 minutes","20 minutes","14 minutes"],"answer":2,"passage_id":null,"audio":"A-l05","formats":["express","balance","deep"]},{"id":"L-B1-001","block":"listening","level":3,"type":"choice","prompt":"What did the man think of the trip?","options":["It was too expensive.","It was spoiled by the rain.","It was boring.","It was great despite the weather."],"answer":3,"passage_id":null,"audio":"A-l06","formats":["express","balance","deep"]},{"id":"L-B1-002","block":"listening","level":3,"type":"choice","prompt":"What will the weather be like in the afternoon?","options":["Rainy","Windy","Warmer and clearer","Colder"],"answer":2,"passage_id":null,"audio":"A-l07","formats":["express","balance","deep"]},{"id":"L-B1-003","block":"listening","level":3,"type":"choice","prompt":"Why does the woman want a new job?","options":["She dislikes her colleagues.","The pay is low.","The work is boring.","The working day is too long."],"answer":3,"passage_id":null,"audio":"A-l08","formats":["express","balance","deep"]},{"id":"L-B2-001","block":"listening","level":4,"type":"choice","prompt":"What surprised the speaker most?","options":["Everyday customs","The climate","The language","The food prices"],"answer":0,"passage_id":null,"audio":"A-l09","formats":["express","balance","deep"]},{"id":"L-B2-002","block":"listening","level":4,"type":"choice","prompt":"Why are morning exercisers more consistent?","options":["They have more energy.","Gyms are cheaper then.","Fewer things interrupt them.","They like mornings."],"answer":2,"passage_id":null,"audio":"A-l10","formats":["express","balance","deep"]},{"id":"L-B2-003","block":"listening","level":4,"type":"choice","prompt":"What is the woman's main concern about the proposal?","options":["The team is too small.","The budget looks unrealistic.","The deadline is too short.","The idea is too risky."],"answer":1,"passage_id":null,"audio":"A-l11","formats":["express","balance","deep"]},{"id":"L-C1-001","block":"listening","level":5,"type":"choice","prompt":"What is the speaker's point?","options":["Too many options can cause anxiety.","People dislike making decisions.","Choice always increases happiness.","Regret is unavoidable."],"answer":0,"passage_id":null,"audio":"A-l12","formats":["express","balance","deep"]},{"id":"L-C1-002","block":"listening","level":5,"type":"choice","prompt":"What is the man's criticism?","options":["His argument was too long.","He made factual errors.","He was badly prepared.","He ignored the main objection."],"answer":3,"passage_id":null,"audio":"A-l13","formats":["express","balance","deep"]},{"id":"L-C1-003","block":"listening","level":5,"type":"choice","prompt":"What does the speaker think of the policy?","options":["It will be popular.","It may defeat its own purpose.","It helps the wrong people.","It is badly explained."],"answer":1,"passage_id":null,"audio":"A-l14","formats":["express","balance","deep"]}],"passages":[{"id":"P-01","level":2,"title":"Maria's weekend","text":"On Saturday, Maria usually gets up late. She has a big breakfast with her sister, and then they go to the market to buy fruit and vegetables. In the afternoon, Maria plays tennis with her friend Olga. On Sunday, she visits her grandparents, who live in a small village near the city. They always cook a special lunch for the family. Maria likes Sundays more than Saturdays because she loves her grandmother's apple cake."},{"id":"P-02","level":3,"title":"Moving to a new city","text":"When Daniel moved to Manchester for work, he didn't know anyone. The first weeks were difficult: he spent most evenings alone in his flat, watching films. Then a colleague invited him to join a local running club. At first Daniel hesitated, as he hadn't run since school, but he decided to try it. Six months later, he has made several close friends and has even signed up for a half-marathon. 'Running wasn't the point,' he says. 'It was a way to meet people.'"},{"id":"P-03","level":3,"title":"A weekend in Lisbon","text":"We arrived in Lisbon on Friday evening and, after checking in, went straight to a small restaurant recommended by the hotel receptionist. The seafood was excellent and surprisingly cheap. On Saturday we took the famous tram up the hills, but it was so crowded that we decided to walk back. That turned out to be the best part of the day, because we found a little cafe with a view over the river. By Sunday, our feet were sore, but we agreed that we would definitely come back."},{"id":"P-04","level":4,"title":"Sleep and memory","text":"Scientists have long known that sleep is essential, but recent research suggests that its role in memory is even greater than previously thought. During deep sleep, the brain appears to replay the day's events, strengthening important connections while discarding trivial details. This may explain why students who sleep after studying perform better in tests than those who stay up revising all night. However, researchers warn against drawing simple conclusions: the amount of sleep people need varies considerably, and for some individuals, six hours may be perfectly adequate."},{"id":"P-05","level":5,"title":"The attention problem","text":"It is tempting to blame our shrinking attention spans on smartphones, but the argument is less straightforward than it appears. Attention has always been a limited resource, and every era has had its distractions; what has changed is the sheer efficiency with which modern technology competes for it. Apps are engineered by teams of specialists whose express aim is to keep users engaged, and against such sophisticated persuasion, individual willpower is a poor defence. This suggests that the burden of responsibility should not rest solely on the user, but also on the designers who profit from our distraction."}],"audios":[{"id":"A-l01","level":1,"src":"assets/leveltest/l01.mp3","duration":17.0},{"id":"A-l02","level":1,"src":"assets/leveltest/l02.mp3","duration":19.0},{"id":"A-l03","level":2,"src":"assets/leveltest/l03.mp3","duration":20.8},{"id":"A-l04","level":2,"src":"assets/leveltest/l04.mp3","duration":19.6},{"id":"A-l05","level":2,"src":"assets/leveltest/l05.mp3","duration":17.4},{"id":"A-l06","level":3,"src":"assets/leveltest/l06.mp3","duration":19.0},{"id":"A-l07","level":3,"src":"assets/leveltest/l07.mp3","duration":20.4},{"id":"A-l08","level":3,"src":"assets/leveltest/l08.mp3","duration":20.3},{"id":"A-l09","level":4,"src":"assets/leveltest/l09.mp3","duration":20.2},{"id":"A-l10","level":4,"src":"assets/leveltest/l10.mp3","duration":21.8},{"id":"A-l11","level":4,"src":"assets/leveltest/l11.mp3","duration":25.2},{"id":"A-l12","level":5,"src":"assets/leveltest/l12.mp3","duration":20.8},{"id":"A-l13","level":5,"src":"assets/leveltest/l13.mp3","duration":21.1},{"id":"A-l14","level":5,"src":"assets/leveltest/l14.mp3","duration":19.7}]}